id: pm-github-curated-reopen-followup
title: Distinguish source-assigned completion dates when curated items reopen
description: "Review follow-up from PR #233 thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62Q98t: preserve completion dates that predate linking, but evaluate clearing dates assigned by a prior GitHub closure when the source reopens. Separate from round-4 durable-state publication; requires explicit provenance for the completion date and real SDK reopen tests."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-github#233",review-followup
created_at: "2026-11-11T18:20:18.830Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T22:07:08.273Z"
author: codex-github230-1111
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-11T22:07:08.272Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 6 review reproduction retained for later work (PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62Q98t): start with a curated linked item with no completed_at, import a GitHub closure so completed_at is assigned from github_closed_at, then reopen the source and re-sync. The item becomes open and closed_at is cleared, but the source-assigned completed_at remains. A pre-link local completion date must still be preserved. Do not clear every completed_at; track source assignment distinctly before implementing reopen cleanup. This round intentionally changes no completion-date behavior."
